A||||10||DXR_DAD||Seat cover cleaning?||||5||
Z||000000||DXR_DAD||02-07-2000||08:01 PM||||I just got a nice set of used seat covers (stock GT) thanks to a fourm member. What is the best way to clean?  Can I just send them to a dry cleaners, Put them in the washer, or can I take just the covers to a detail shop before I install them?<P>THANKS||||reg||5
Z||000001||ggarsk||02-07-2000||11:03 PM||||Mr. Mike knows how to wash them. I guess if you e-mail him he'll send you the instructions. I got a good used seat cover that needs washing so I'll e-mail him and post the intructions here.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||02-08-2000||01:50 AM||||Glad you liked the covers. I cleaned them last spring. I used a portable steam cleaner called "The little green machine" It did an "OK" job but I hear Dirt Devil has a small one out that has rotating brushes which should do a better job. The another way is to buy some upolstery spray cleaner and a auto parts place and use damp soft brush to scrub them.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||02-08-2000||11:35 AM||||Thanks Oreif, those covers were in darn good shape. I think I'll just try to wash them. I thought about getting a little green machine I saw then on sale at K-Mart some time ago.||||reg||14
Z||000004||ggarsk||02-08-2000||07:58 PM||||DXR_DAD, I just got a reply from Mr.Mike. You just wash the covers with Tide and hot water. He didn't say but I would guess on gentle cycle. Then hang dry....putting them in the dryer will ruin the foam. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||02-08-2000||08:20 PM||||Thanks ggarsk, I'm on it as we speak, they should  be on the spin cycle. I'll let you know how they turn out.<P>Once again, I just say thanks to everyone enough everyone on this fourm has been a big help to me and my little black plastic toy!!<P>Oreif, thanks again for a nice set of covers at a nice price too!!!||||reg||14
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||02-09-2000||09:59 AM||||THEY LOOK NEW!!  like a new born babies butt,<BR>I soaked them in stain remover, spray and wash, used a brush to scrub a bit, let them soak in the tub, then put them in the washer.<BR>I did put them in the dryer (air no heat).<P>Thanks||||reg||14
Z||000007||ggarsk||02-09-2000||10:55 AM||||That's cool...I'll be washing mine this weekend.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DXR_DAD||02-12-2000||08:11 PM||||Oreif, I got the covers on the seats. Thanks for the tape it helped alot. My passenger side was in excellent shape, so it was the driver side that needed the recover. I did use the bottom cover from yours on my passenger side. The rain just started so I"ll just leave them in the living room, The look good in there anyway   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and spray them with some scotch guard.<P>ggarsk, did you get to yours yet?  now I need to clean the carpet   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I will have pics soon<P>thanks guys!!!<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 02-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||02-12-2000||10:56 PM||||DXR_DAD, Glad everything worked out for you.<BR>Just in case you decide to go to leather, you can save the old emblems if you want to transfer them to the leather seats. I just had mine embriodered with the logo. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||ggarsk||02-14-2000||11:05 PM||||I just washed my seat cover. Looks like new. I won't be putting it on for a while...got to much other stuff to do.||||reg||1
